        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive collection requirement stood up against PRC cyber pre-positioning activities targeting U.S. critical infrastructure, with particular emphasis on facilities and communications nodes in the Indo-Pacific region including Guam. The requirement should task SIGINT, cyber threat intelligence, and liaison channels with private-sector network defenders to identify and characterize intrusion sets assessed to be staging for disruptive or destructive effects against U.S. military logistics, power grid, telecommunications, and transportation networks. Collection should also cover PRC command-and-control infrastructure that could enable rapid escalation to offensive cyber operations in a crisis scenario, as well as any indicators that Beijing is shifting from espionage-focused access to pre-positioned destructive payloads. Additionally, we want a secondary line of collection on PRC transnational cyber operations targeting diaspora communities, journalists, and dissidents outside China's borders, particularly any technical overlaps with the infrastructure-focused intrusion sets. All nominated sources and methods should be validated against current ODNI threat assessment priorities, and initial nominations should be coordinated through the Cyber Threat Intelligence Integration Center within two weeks. Final collection plans should specify expected cadence of reporting, deconfliction with FBI and CISA equities on domestic critical infrastructure, and any allied partnership channels available for corroboration. Classification guidance should follow existing PRC cyber operations tear-line standards.",
